{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "QueryPie permissions and records do not remove old direct database routes automatically. Where users should connect is an important adoption decision too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I queried the same order directly and through QueryPie in DBeaver, then closed the direct port. A new QueryPie connection still returned the order and was audited."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Preparing the Comparison Database and Read Access"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I created a separate MySQL with three fictional orders, registered it as DB Route Lab, and gave route_reader read-only table access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After Test Connection succeeded, I hid database credentials from user lists and configured proxy access to use the registered account."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Proxy using registered credentials and query auditing enabled.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Proxy using registered credentials and query auditing enabled."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Developer received Read-Only on DB Route Lab. Registration and user authorization were separate: administrators manage credentials; users choose permitted connections."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Developer given read-only access to the new lab database.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Developer given read-only access to the new lab database."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Creating Direct and QueryPie Connections in DBeaver"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Direct access used 127.0.0.1:13307 on the Mac; QueryPie used 127.0.0.1:40002 from Proxy Info. Both reached route_lab."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Checking the QueryPie proxy address and port.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Checking the QueryPie proxy address and port."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used Demo Developer’s proxy token for Agentless Proxy in DBeaver. User-facing credentials identify the person; QueryPie’s registered account connects to the database."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The direct query returned order 27002, SHIPPED, amount 18,500. I used this as the baseline for the same SQL through QueryPie."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Order 27002 queried through a direct database connection.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Order 27002 queried through a direct database connection."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Same SQL Works Through QueryPie"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ID, status, and amount matched. Running SQL and inspecting the result grid in DBeaver felt unchanged."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. The same order returned through QueryPie.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. The same order returned through QueryPie."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Users could keep existing tools while administrators managed their privileges centrally. Issued proxy credentials replaced distributing the database password to each user."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Closing the Direct Database Port"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I disconnected both DBeaver connections, removed the Docker port published to Mac at 13307, and recreated the lab container while retaining data and internal networking."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Closing the port is Docker networking work. QueryPie handles authentication, privileges, and SQL audits on the remaining proxy route. Both network paths and user access are being managed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A new direct connection returned ‘Connection refused (connect failed).’ Stored database credentials could not create a connection to the closed address."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. New direct connection refused after removing the published port.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. New direct connection refused after removing the published port."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reconnecting Through QueryPie Preserves Queries and Audits"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A new DBeaver QueryPie connection returned order 27002 with the same SHIPPED and 18,500."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. A new QueryPie connection still reads the order after direct access closes.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. A new QueryPie connection still reads the order after direct access closes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Query Audit showed SELECT Success, Demo Developer, DB Route Lab, Read-Only, and Executed From Agentless Proxy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-connection-path/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Proxy read’s user, privileges, database, and SQL in the audit.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Proxy read’s user, privileges, database, and SQL in the audit."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The database account was route_reader, while QueryPie also identified Demo Developer. SQL for order 27002 and time were retained, linking database identity and actual requester in one view."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Centralizing Access Without Replacing the Tool"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The user’s work changed little. DBeaver queries stayed the same; after routing through QueryPie, user privileges and activity became visible centrally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This combines network restrictions on direct access with QueryPie’s user-based authorization. Teams keep familiar tools while access and activity are organized by person."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7, DBeaver 26.2.4, a separate MySQL, and fictional orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
